title ALES21 — Lotus's markers in real time, a named place set and read in seconds
prompt Autonomous loop past REMEMBER + the itineraries — take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment, stop at the custody gates. baton prin recur.
think ALES20 (the markers track) landed by raw sample index; a musician marks the downbeat by TIME, not by counting samples. ALES14's loop already learned this (mark_ms sets loop points in seconds through the ALES5 clock); this rung gives markers the same twin. Crux-first: real-time marking is the smallest durable move that makes the whole markers track usable by a musician who lives in time, composing ALES20's add and ALES5's samples_for/ms_for over public APIs with no new arithmetic — the exact mirror of a proven move, least risk of the road-on's rungs. Wholly within the read side, no seam, no gate.
think The crux and why it is EXACT: a place set in seconds lands at exactly samples_for(ms) and reads back the honestly-lossy same time; the track stays sorted and unique by ALES20's own add invariant. The conversion is ALES5's proven samples_for (bounded, refusing DurationTooLong past the clip), handed to markers.add with no new bound; reading back is clock.ms_for, honestly lossy exactly as ALES5 defines (at one sample per ms, exact).
think Reuse over reinvention: clock.samples_for/ms_for and markers.add/pos_of reused whole; markers.rye stays pure sample-index, this rung only adds a time face (mark_ms, pos_ms) over it — the stereo_transport-stands-on-transport pattern. New file marker_time.rye per rung. No usize, no @memcpy, no qualified assert.
think First build GREEN but the DurationTooLong case was miswritten: huge_ms = max_clip at 1 sample/ms converts to exactly max_clip samples (allowed, not > max_clip), so add tripped PastEnd not DurationTooLong — the witness caught it (WrongDuration). Fixed to max_clip + 1 ms, which converts to max_clip + 1 samples, one past the clip bound, so samples_for throws DurationTooLong before add is reached. Second run GREEN. A good catch by the witness — the edge test now proves the real clock edge, not an aliased one.
obs GREEN on the second run across three blocks: places set at 300/100/250/0 ms out of order read ascending samples 0,100,250,300, each reading its ms back exactly and carrying its name; the edges refused PastEnd (501ms past a 500-sample master), DurationTooLong (max_clip+1 ms past the clip), and Duplicate (two places at 200ms); two timed places drove a real region_between (armed loop [100,400) span 300) and a scrub snap landed exactly on the 400-sample mark.
obs tame_style_check exit 0 (bans clean); the new module carries asserts on both functions, off the zero-assert ratchet.
loom witness=ales_marker_time_witness cases=3 clock_rate=1000 result=GREEN build=second-run
file lotus/marker_time.rye ALES21 module — the time face over ALES20's markers, the twin of loop.mark_ms.
file tools/ales_marker_time_witness.rish the witness proving ALES21 GREEN on metal.
file active-designing/20260814-fill-ales21-lotus-marker-time.md the self-approved design round for ALES21.
file lotus/README.md status line, rung bullet, and road-on updated for ALES21.
recommend keep-going ALES22 can offer the choice of pan/crossfade law where a crossfade meets a marked edit, or name a selection (a marked span cut or gained as one) — both agent-doable, no custody gate. A punch region armed between two timed markers, tying playback to the Mikrophone's capture, is a module seam that waits for Keaton's word.
